# The player's MIDI map (0.16.11): a map learned in the emulator and sent from the Install page (midimap.bin, made by web/fm1backup.js mmEncode: a pad
# note 36 on channel 10 is PLAY, CC 20 a fader on SELECT, CC 21 an encoder (64 +- n) on knob 1, CC 22 a button on SEQ, middle C the first key).
# It is checked as a restore is, loaded at boot, and a learned message acts as the panel's own, before anything else MIDI does.
seed 0
loadobj 24 tests/scenarios/midimap.bin
restore 24
expect rsvalid 1
restore 24 bad
expect rsvalid 0
reboot
wait 3000
expect playing 1
# the pad: PLAY pressed and let go
midi 99 24 7F
wait 60
midi 89 24 00
wait 200
expect playing 0
midi 99 24 64
wait 60
midi 99 24 00
wait 200
expect playing 1
# the fader on SELECT: from 40 up to 46, three clicks (a click every two steps; the dial takes a quick burst as one page, so a step at a time)
expect view 0
midi B0 14 28
wait 150
midi B0 14 2A
wait 150
midi B0 14 2C
wait 150
midi B0 14 2E
wait 200
expect view 3
# and back down, a step at a time
midi B0 14 2C
wait 150
midi B0 14 2A
wait 150
midi B0 14 28
wait 200
expect view 0
# the encoder on knob 1 (Tempo's page: the tempo), 64 + 3
setpar 5 120
wait 100
midi B0 15 43
wait 200
expect par5 123
midi B0 15 3E
wait 200
expect par5 121
# CC 22 held: SEQ held (0.4 s: the sequencer); let go
midi B0 16 7F
wait 700
expect view 34
midi B0 16 00
wait 200
tap HOME
wait 200
expect view 0
